WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.260
- America is the freest,

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.750
most freedomful country
in the entire world,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.180
despite what some hack
YouTube lawyer says.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.040
And for those traveling
internationally for the first time,

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.180
you may be surprised to learn

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.340
that many American rights,
freedoms, and values

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.500
are not universally held abroad.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.700
In fact, one country's liberty

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.590
can be another country's crime.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.140
But in fact, we Americans
are so constantly surrounded

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.110
by so much freedom that we
often just take it for granted,

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.970
like David Foster Wallace's metaphor.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.790
One fish asks another,
"How's the water today?"

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.340
And the other fish
shoots him with an AR-15.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.810
And if you've spent your entire life

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.310
in the land of the free
and home of the brave,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.290
it can be easy to overlook
the other countries

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.330
that are, in fact, not America.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.310
There are tons of rights and activities

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.230
that are perfectly legal
in the United States

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.730
but could land you in some hot water

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.440
if you tried it in another country,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.530
like the mullet hairstyle, for example.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.330
The mullet, that iconic hairstyle

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.360
of 1980s actors, rock stars and athletes,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.440
really has no business

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.900
continuing to exist in the 21st century,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.660
and yet, inexplicably, it still does.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.100
But this is America, dammit,

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.050
where you don't have
to fight for your right

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.410
to party in the back and
business in the front.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.330
But if you wanna cosplay as Joe Dirt,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.080
or compete in the USA
Mullet Championships,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.480
yes, that is a very real
thing that people do,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.620
then it is your right as an
American to look like an idiot.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.660
In fact, that might be
the most fundamental

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.280
American right that there is.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.900
But for certain freedom-hating countries

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.700
trying to save you from yourselves,

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.920
the mullet and other crimes of fashion

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.780
constitute a criminal offense.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.630
For example, in 2010,
Iran's Ministry of Culture

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.400
officially said goodbye to mullets,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.710
banning the hairstyle
for being un-Islamic.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.030
In an effort to rid the country

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.430
of so-called decadent Western haircuts,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.380
Iran launched a crackdown on mullets,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.880
elaborate spikes, and long hair,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.240
because nothing says
decadence like the mullet.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.650
Now, in years leading up to the ban,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.210
police have actually raided barbershops

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.520
that offer these disfavored hairstyles.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.530
After the ban, violators
have been subject to fines

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.090
and impromptu haircuts by the police

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.920
for violating these standards.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.270
Government officials have even gone

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.680
to hairdressing trade shows

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.050
to outline what haircuts are legal.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.720
Also, in 2021, North
Korea launched own war

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.000
against mullets and other foreign styles.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.900
In an effort to crack down

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.610
on so-called non-socialist hairdos,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.810
the rogue communist country

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.910
outlawed mullets and spiky, dyed hair,

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.190
while also enlisting the state-run

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.870
Socialist Patriotic Youth League

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.680
to act as literal fashion
police against the banned cuts.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.660
Nose and lip piercings, skinny jeans,

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.790
and branded T-shirts were also outlawed.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.670
And though this is hardly the
worst human rights violation

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.620
of this repressive regime,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.410
it seems like Kim Jung Un is in no place

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.440
to prosecute anyone for
ridiculous haircuts.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.480
And it's not just hairstyles
that don't make the cut.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.700
Pun 100% intended.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.290
In the nation of Tajikistan,

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.410
the secular government
has waged a war on beards

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.490
in an effort to crack down on what it sees

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.040
as the influence of Islamic radicalism.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.100
In the country, only clean-shaven
men can get passports,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.310
and beards are often forcibly
shaved off by police officers.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.930
So if you're a hirsute hipster

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.700
looking to open up that barbershop

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.250
just for that ironic beard and mustache,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.560
you'll have to look outside of Tajikistan.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.810
But obviously you've already set up shop

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.670
in Williamsburg anyway.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.690
But just because it's legal

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.760
to get a really terrible
haircut in the United States

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.000
doesn't mean that you won't
be subject to a good spanking,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.890
unless you're outside
of the United States,

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.510
because when it comes to raising children,

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.530
there's a fierce debate

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.660
as to whether parents
should spank their kids.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.077
Some parents live by the adage,

00:03:20.077 --> 00:03:22.560
"Use your words, not your
hands," while other parents,

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.840
particularly those influenced
by older generations,

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.277
live by the biblically-inspired aphorism,

00:03:27.277 --> 00:03:29.580
"Spare the rod, spoil the child."

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.290
But as a strictly legal matter

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.480
here in the grand old US of A,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.970
the right to spank your
kids shall not be infringed.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.010
In fact, the use of corporal punishment

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.090
on one's own children,

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.500
defined as spanking, paddling,

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.060
or other forms of physical punishment

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.530
to correct misbehavior,

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.510
is protected by law in all 50 states

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.340
plus the District of Columbia.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.800
Now, for those of us whose
parents spanked us as kids,

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.360
that probably doesn't surprise you.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.520
What might surprise you in
most of the United States

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.070
is that it remains
perfectly legal for teachers

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.600
to paddle children in school,

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.870
and not just in Springfield
Elementary School.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.290
- Talking out of turn, that's a paddling.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.920
Looking out the window, that's a paddling.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.200
- In fact, in 1977, the
Supreme Court upheld

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.030
the constitutionality of school spankings.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.530
In Ingraham versus Wright,

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.380
the court ruled 5-4 that paddling
children in public schools

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.030
did not violate the Eighth Amendment's ban

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.980
on cruel and unusual punishment.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.170
As a result, the Supreme
Court left it up to the states

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.610
to decide whether to allow spanking

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.560
in educational settings or to ban it.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.937
- Huh?

00:04:26.937 --> 00:04:27.876
- Hell yeah!

00:04:27.876 --> 00:04:31.830
(students gasping)
(ominous music)

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.420
- And today, 19 US states

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.340
still allow public school personnel

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.340
to use corporal punishment from
preschool to the 12th grade.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.070
And for private schools,
corporal punishment remains legal

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:44.250
in every US state except
New Jersey and Iowa.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.100
But outside the United States,
there has been a clear trend

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.650
not merely to dissuade
parents from spanking children

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.600
but to actually make the practice illegal.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.030
In 1979, Sweden became the first country

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.040
to explicitly ban spanking.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.080
This was wildly controversial at the time,

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.360
sparking contentious debate
about parental rights

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.040
versus state responsibilities,

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.587
and some Swedish headlines
at the time included, quote,

00:05:05.587 --> 00:05:07.320
"Swedes have gone mad,"

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.080
and, "The government takes
charge of parenting in Sweden."

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.390
But over the past four decades,
the trend against spanking

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.550
has been on the rise all over the world.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.070
In fact, according to the
American Spanking Institute,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.500
in conjunction with Mothers
for Hand Smacking...

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.420
I'm just kidding. I made
both of those just up.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.650
You gotta stay on your toes.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.660
No, I mean, according
to the Global Initiative

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.970
to End All Corporal
Punishment Of Children,

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.550
a total of 63 countries
have made smacking children

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.250
illegal in any setting, including at home.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.370
Countries on this list span
five continents, and in 2022,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.770
Wales became the latest
country to ban the practice.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.170
And the bans are even more
numerous in school settings,

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.430
with corporal punishment in schools

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.980
now outlawed in 135 countries.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.008
- Ooh, you better believe
that's a paddling.

00:05:46.008 --> 00:05:47.490
(Lisa groans)

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.050
- Decades after Sweden's ban,

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.360
anti-spanking advocates
can point to hard data

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.430
that suggested a direct correlation

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:56.250
between spanking bans and
better-adjusted children.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.083
But that being said,

00:05:57.083 --> 00:05:58.890
the prospect of actually
prohibiting spanking at home

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.630
remains unlikely in the United States,

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.330
as many consider such a ban
to be an oppressive intrusion

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.310
by the state into parental rights.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:06.990
And even in the 21st century,

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:09.690
spanking in the US has its
share of high-profile defenders,

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.850
particularly on the
conservative side of the aisle.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.850
- I got hit with a strap. Bam, bam, bam!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.650
And I've never been to a shrink.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.170
- In 2014, Fox News
commentator, Sean Hannity,

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.690
famously defended parents'
rights to spank their children,

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.010
citing his own upbringing

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:26.370
by beating the desk with a
belt to a confused panel.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.167
- I got it like this. (grunts)

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.570
And I deserved it. I was a trouble kid.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.950
- Now, notwithstanding the views

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.630
of the obviously
well-adjusted commentator,

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.490
who clearly turned out fine,

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.610
spanking has seen a
notable decline in the US.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.560
The proportion of parents
who utilize the practices

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.000
dropped from 50% in 1993
to only 35% in 2017.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.260
But look, if you want your children

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.580
to turn out like Sean Hannity,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.190
then maybe start with some spankings.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.770
But that takes us to a topic
that almost everyone agrees on,

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.510
and that is cannabis,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.490
because in a nation that
seems increasingly divided

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.050
on almost every single issue,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.970
one of the few areas
of bipartisan agreement

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.370
is the embrace of legal marijuana.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:05.250
Now, although cannabis remains
illegal under federal law,

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.990
the feds have allowed states to experiment

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.570
with their own loosen
restrictions, because, well,

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.940
well, I'll let John
Mulaney explain that one.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.840
- With weed, it was just
something we wanted really badly,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.180
and we kept asking them for 40 years.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.434
Like, "'Scuse me."

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.090
(audience laughing)

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:24.420
And then suddenly the government
became, like, cool parents,

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.887
and they're just like,
"Okay, here, take a little."

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.480
We'd rather you do it in the
house than go somewhere else.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.980
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah."

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.540
- But that being said,
Customs and Border Patrol

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.040
works tirelessly to prevent drugs

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.300
from entering this country.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.370
Like the time that they
celebrated the interdiction

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.670
of this massive haul of drugs
from entering American shores.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.080
Thank you for your service.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.530
But as of 2022, recreational
marijuana is currently legal

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.480
in 18 states, DC, and Guam,

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.420
31 states plus DC have
decriminalized low-level offenses,

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.870
and a whopping 37 states
allow it for medical use.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.670
With public support for full legalization

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.890
standing at a record 68%,

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.690
Americans certainly have come a long way

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.850
since the days of reefer madness.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.280
- [Narrator] Innocently they dance,

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.560
innocent of a new and deadly menace

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.933
lurking behind closed doors.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:18.540
Marijuana, the burning weed
with its roots in hell.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.210
- But try to take that wacky
tobacky outside of our borders

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.400
and you could find yourself
in severe legal jeopardy.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.070
In fact, in a handful of
countries, possession of cannabis

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.650
could have you staring
down a hangman's noose.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.870
And this disparate legal
treatment of cannabis abroad

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.860
was recently put on display

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.410
following a high-profile
detention in Putin's Russia.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.640
In February 2022,

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.220
US women's basketball
superstar, Brittney Griner,

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:41.100
was arrested after customs
authorities claimed to have found

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.550
cannabis vape oil cartridges
in her carry-on bag.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.050
But given that Griner's arrest

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.360
came days before Russia invaded Ukraine,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.760
some have speculated that the
Kremlin arrested Ms. Griner

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.530
to pressure the US and others

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.020
to not stand in the way
of Putin's invasion.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.520
To that point, Russia has been known

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.130
to falsify drug charges
against critics in the past,

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.650
so it's certainly not out
of the realm of possibility

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.540
that the same happened here.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.640
I guess she should just
consider herself lucky

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.180
that she wasn't poisoned
with a radioactive substance.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.410
But while a few dozen countries

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.670
have relaxed restrictions on the plant,

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.440
the recreational medical use of cannabis

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.140
remains very illegal in the
vast majority of nations.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.660
For example, in 2021,

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.530
24-year-old British
soccer coach, Billy Hood,

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.360
was arrested in the United Arab Emirates

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.450
with four bottles of
CBD vape oil in his car.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.970
Local authorities charged Mr.
Hood with drug trafficking,

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.820
and then sentenced him to
25 years in a Dubai prison.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:32.070
Mr. Hood's sentence was then
reduced to 10 years on appeal,

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.720
but he remains incarcerated,

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.990
In 2013, Egypt executed
Charles Raymond Ferndale,

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.370
a 74-year-old British citizen,

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.040
for allegedly smuggling
three tons of hashish,

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.140
which Ferndale insisted until his death

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.810
that he had been tricked
into doing by third parties.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.920
In 2021, Singapore's sentenced
Omar Yacob Bamadhaj to death

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.720
for bringing at least
two pounds of cannabis

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.040
into the country in 2018.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.260
And like Ferndale, his
lawyers also argued,

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.750
he did not knowingly bring
drugs into the country.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:58.830
Though, despite America's

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.810
comparatively looser pot restrictions,

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.210
America still has over 40,000 people

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.040
in jail for marijuana offenses,

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.960
something that absolutely requires fixing.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.660
And even with these disparities,
at the very least, though,

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.920
toking up in the United States

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.870
will not result in the death sentence.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.430
But that's something that
you can change in America,

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.810
because you have the right to vote,

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.000
but you also have the right to not vote

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.260
if you don't want to,

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.820
because while millions of Americans

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.910
stand up every election day
to have their voices heard,

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.150
millions of Americans also
choose to sit down, stay home,

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:29.370
and deliberately not vote at all.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.780
- If I were registered to vote,

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.370
I'd send these clowns a message

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.900
by staying home on election day

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.460
and dressing up like a clown.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.980
- Now, it might seem obvious
to say that you have the right

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.590
not to participate in American elections,

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.610
but it might surprise you to learn

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:42.750
that staying home on election day

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.330
is actually illegal in
over two dozen countries.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.950
That's right, in 27 countries,

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.930
all eligible citizens are required by law

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.660
to register and vote in
every single election.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.430
Though, several countries, like Chile,

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:55.140
Italy, and the Dominican Republic,

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.970
that previously adopted mandatory voting,

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.040
have since abandoned the practice.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.900
A handful of countries
with compulsory voting

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.300
don't actually enforce any
penalty for failure to vote,

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.340
like Bulgaria, Costa Rica, and Mexico,

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.320
but over a dozen countries
enforce a penalty

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:09.270
for failing to vote in elections.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.950
Some countries penalize non-voters

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.660
with outright disenfranchisement.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.520
In Singapore, a voter
that misses an election

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.680
is removed from voting
roles and must re-register

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.780
and submit a valid reason for not voting.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.160
Other countries issue fines,

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.260
and can even result in jail time.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.150
Brazil requires all eligible citizens,

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.410
excluding the illiterate,

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.500
voters aged 16 and 17, and those aged 70,

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.310
to vote or be subject to
a fine of less than $1.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:34.560
In Australia, citizens
are legally required

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.670
to go to their polling place,

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.640
but can choose to decline to
participate after signing in.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.680
However, failure to show up
at the polling place at all

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:44.790
can subject Aussies to a fine
of 100 didgeridoos, probably,

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.220
or the equivalent of
$14 to $34 US dollars,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.370
and citizens who repeatedly
refuse to pay the small fine

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:51.630
can actually go to jail.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.490
Among countries with
compulsory voting laws,

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.860
there are those that tie voting
directly to your pocketbook.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.540
For example, in Peru,

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.550
a voter must have a stamped voting card

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.770
to obtain certain services and goods

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.540
from some public offices.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.373
And in Bolivia,

00:12:04.373 --> 00:12:06.390
a voter is given a card
to prove participation,

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.460
and a citizen who cannot
show proof of voting

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.290
within three months after the election

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:14.130
will be ineligible to receive
a salary from the bank.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.810
Advocates for this compulsory system

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:18.510
liken the democratic participation
to civil responsibilities

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:21.300
like taxation, jury duty,
and military service,

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.920
and argue that participating in democracy

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.900
is a duty instead of a right.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:27.090
Others argue that forcing people to vote

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.590
compels higher voter turnout,

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:32.370
as Australia rarely falls
below 90% participation,

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.650
while Brazil's most recent
presidential election

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.480
was just below 80%.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.950
And compare that to the United States,

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.210
where voter turnout struggles

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.340
to crack 50% in a midterm election,

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:44.820
and only occasionally breaks
60% in presidential contests.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.470
However, the idea of
forcing people to vote

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.240
and punishing them for nonparticipation

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.100
is not a popular concept

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.440
among nations with voluntary suffrage.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:55.020
Critics see voting as a civic
right rather than a duty,

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.760
and contend that forcing someone to vote

00:12:56.760 --> 00:13:00.450
is counter to the very idea
of liberty and free choice.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.160
And some American legal scholars contend

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:04.560
that mandatory voting laws would
constitute compelled speech

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:05.970
that violates the First Amendment,

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.310
as the right to speak necessarily involves

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:09.720
the freedom not to speak.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.670
So as long as you live
in the United States,

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.407
you can rest assured of your
constitutional right to say,

00:13:14.407 --> 00:13:15.761
"None of the above."

00:13:15.761 --> 00:13:16.594
- The only thing not silly

00:13:16.594 --> 00:13:18.540
is the power of the people's vote.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:21.023
And I think the people
should use it to vote for

00:13:21.023 --> 00:13:22.770
(triumphant music)
